# Charts of Rehan needs NO credentials.
#
# This file exists so that an operator looking for the usual "where do I put the
# API key" answer finds a written one instead of guessing. The service reads:
#
#   * local files it already owns (the market-feed recording under data/), and
#   * public exchange pages, with a polite rate limit and a cache.
#
# It never logs in anywhere, never holds a token, and never calls an
# authenticated endpoint. If a future source needs a credential, it is set as an
# environment variable in the deployment environment and NEVER committed here.
#
# Optional runtime knobs (all have defaults; nothing below is a secret):
#
# CHART_SERVICE_PORT=8788          # loopback port for `python -m charts`
# CHART_SERVICE_INTERVAL=15        # seconds between polls per watched symbol
# CHART_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
